  "body": "Guest bookings previously selected an existing Party by email and could change that account\u2019s contact details. Payable checkout created contacts before its request lock, allowing duplicate or orphan contacts. Marketplace manual-evidence retries also need to preserve the contact already attached to the checkout.\n\nCreate unverified guest contacts inside the owning transaction after locking and replay checks. Booking retries return the same booking. Marketplace evidence reuses the locked checkout\u2019s recorded contact, supports corrections after rejection, rejects identity conflicts, and rolls back contact creation if dependent writes fail. Shared email does not establish account ownership.\n\nDepends on #434. Validation passed: focused account-isolation Hspec; real PostgreSQL HTTP booking concurrency/replay/resource-conflict tests; four marketplace PostgreSQL regressions covering concurrent evidence, retries, rejection/correction, absent payment selection, and dependent audit failure rollback. Financial-effect assertions remain zero. No schema change or production deployment in this PR. See docs/identity/guest-booking-prevention.md.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-09-18T07:46:05Z",
